# ==== T-FMT-D (R41) fill-pack matrix — BROKEN-ELEMENT axis.
#
# SUBJECT: this fixture asserts `gg fmt` OUTPUT (byte-for-byte, in
# `fmt_fill_pack_broken_element_axis`) — a bulk `gg fmt` sweep MUST EXCLUDE it.
#
# Cells sampled (Core #12 — this file samples the `broken element` axis ONLY):
#   be_resume  a MULTI-LINE element among flat siblings. The packer cannot
#              measure it flat, so it BREAKS to the continuation indent before it
#              — exactly the column plain `doc::surround` used to place every
#              element at, and exactly the column `element_to_string`
#              pre-rendered it for — and then RESUMES packing after it.
#   be_nested  FILL-INSIDE-FILL composition: the multi-line element is itself a
#              filled list, pre-rendered one indent level deeper.
#
# NOT sampled here — a genuine `Doc::HardLine` INSIDE a `Doc::Fill`: no
# `format_expr` path can produce one (every `surround_fill` item is a
# `doc::text(..)` leaf built from `element_to_string`, and `text` never carries a
# HardLine). That cell is pinned at the algebra level instead, by
# `test_fill_hardline_element_breaks_and_packing_resumes` in
# `src/formatter/doc.rs`.
#
# KNOWN, PRE-EXISTING blind spot these cells also document: a nested element is
# pre-rendered by a sub-formatter that starts at column 0 and knows only its
# INDENT LEVEL, so its own internal packing ignores the column it is finally
# placed at. Breaking before every multi-line element keeps that error exactly
# where plain `doc::surround` had it (the element always starts at the
# continuation indent) rather than making it worse — but the element's interior
# lines can still exceed the budget, and the wired test names them.
#
# RED source: both rows are TRUE pre-fix REDs — pre-fix the OUTER lists explode
# one element per line, so "flat siblings share the open line" never happens and
# the packing never resumes after the multi-line element.
void be_resume():
    outer(aaaa, bbbb, inner(1111111, 2222222, 3333333, 4444444, 5555555, 6666666, 7777777, 8888888, 9999999, 1010101, 1111011, 1212121, 1313131, 1414141, 1515151, 1616161), cccc, dddd)

void be_nested():
    Vector[int] v = [111111, 222222, [1111111, 2222222, 3333333, 4444444, 5555555, 6666666, 7777777, 8888888, 9999999, 1010101, 1111011, 1212121, 1313131, 1414141, 1515151, 1616161], 333333]
